<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 176 0 R
/T (Managing an Information Systems project reinforced that effective control depends on continuous evidence rather than initial plans alone. Through the FlowBikes case study I learned that risk registers and schedule dependency diagrams become useful only when they are kept current with dated progress updates, revised effort figures, and documented corrective actions.)
/E (Managing an Information Systems project reinforced that effective control depends on continuous evidence rather than initial plans alone. Through the FlowBikes case study I learned that risk registers and schedule dependency diagrams become useful only when they are kept current with dated progress updates, revised effort figures, and documented corrective actions.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
